1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:19,931
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June sixteenth. On the evening of the sixteenth, a strong earthquake hit the Kanto region near Tokyo. Two prefectures felt a level five-weak quake, but there was no danger of a tsunami. Let's listen.

2
00:00:20,532 --> 00:00:23,292
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:23,992 --> 00:00:30,544
[News] 16日の夜、関東地方で大きな地震がありました。

4
00:00:31,243 --> 00:00:39,595
[News] 午後7時46分ごろ、茨城県の南部を震源とする地震が起きました。

5
00:00:40,295 --> 00:00:47,591
[News] 群馬県と埼玉県では、最大で震度5弱を観測しました。

6
00:00:48,292 --> 00:00:53,859
[News] 強い揺れで、棚から物が落ちた家もありました。

7
00:00:54,560 --> 00:01:00,896
[News] 地震の大きさを表すマグニチュードは、5.5でした。

8
00:01:01,595 --> 00:01:06,444
[News] この地震による津波の心配はありません。

9
00:01:07,144 --> 00:01:14,512
[News] 今のところ、大きなけがや、建物の被害は報告されていません。

10
00:01:15,212 --> 00:01:24,043
[News] 気象庁は、これから1週間ほど、強い地震に注意するように呼びかけています。

11
00:01:24,743 --> 00:01:31,200
[News] 揺れの強かった地域の人は、安全に気をつけてください。

12
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:33,531
[Host] Let's break it down.

13
00:01:34,132 --> 00:01:41,620
[Slow] 16日の夜、関東地方で大きな地震がありました。

14
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:47,123
[Host] On the evening of the sixteenth, there was a big earthquake in the Kanto region.

15
00:01:47,724 --> 00:01:49,956
[Vocab] 地震

16
00:01:50,355 --> 00:01:58,203
[Host] It means earthquake. The first character means earth or ground, the second means to shake — the ground shaking.

17
00:01:58,804 --> 00:02:08,331
[Slow] 午後7時46分ごろ、茨城県の南部を震源とする地震が起きました。

18
00:02:09,132 --> 00:02:16,836
[Host] At around seven forty-six in the evening, an earthquake occurred with its epicenter in southern Ibaraki Prefecture.

19
00:02:17,436 --> 00:02:19,788
[Vocab] 震源

20
00:02:20,187 --> 00:02:28,611
[Host] It means the epicenter — the underground point where an earthquake begins. The first character is quake, the second is source.

21
00:02:29,211 --> 00:02:37,539
[Slow] 群馬県と埼玉県では、最大で震度5弱を観測しました。

22
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:44,627
[Host] In Gunma and Saitama Prefectures, they measured a maximum of level five-weak.

23
00:02:45,228 --> 00:02:47,460
[Vocab] 震度

24
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:59,692
[Host] It means seismic intensity — how strongly the ground shakes at a place, on Japan's zero-to-seven scale. Don't confuse it with magnitude, which is the size of the quake itself.

25
00:03:00,292 --> 00:03:06,651
[Slow] 強い揺れで、棚から物が落ちた家もありました。

26
00:03:07,451 --> 00:03:11,987
[Host] With the strong shaking, in some homes things fell off the shelves.

27
00:03:12,587 --> 00:03:14,532
[Vocab] 揺れ

28
00:03:14,931 --> 00:03:22,324
[Host] It means shaking or a tremor. It's the noun from the verb to sway, to shake — the motion you actually feel.

29
00:03:22,924 --> 00:03:28,443
[Slow] この地震による津波の心配はありません。

30
00:03:29,243 --> 00:03:32,651
[Host] There is no danger of a tsunami from this earthquake.

31
00:03:33,252 --> 00:03:35,412
[Vocab] 津波

32
00:03:35,812 --> 00:03:44,883
[Host] It means tsunami — a giant sea wave that an undersea quake can cause. It's already an English word, borrowed straight from Japanese.

33
00:03:45,484 --> 00:03:53,883
[Slow] 今のところ、大きなけがや、建物の被害は報告されていません。

34
00:03:54,683 --> 00:03:59,939
[Host] So far, no serious injuries or damage to buildings have been reported.

35
00:04:00,539 --> 00:04:02,651
[Vocab] 被害

36
00:04:03,051 --> 00:04:13,084
[Host] It means damage or harm — the loss caused by a disaster or accident. You'll hear it constantly in news about storms, floods, and quakes.

37
00:04:13,683 --> 00:04:23,788
[Slow] 気象庁は、これから1週間ほど、強い地震に注意するように呼びかけています。

38
00:04:24,588 --> 00:04:30,540
[Host] The Meteorological Agency is urging people to watch out for strong earthquakes for about a week.

39
00:04:31,139 --> 00:04:33,732
[Vocab] 呼びかける

40
00:04:34,132 --> 00:04:45,028
[Host] It means to call on people, to urge — to publicly ask everyone to do something. It literally combines to call and to hang, like sending a call out to the crowd.

41
00:04:45,627 --> 00:04:53,019
[Slow] 揺れの強かった地域の人は、安全に気をつけてください。

42
00:04:53,819 --> 00:04:58,379
[Host] People in areas with strong shaking, please take care to stay safe.

43
00:04:58,980 --> 00:05:01,139
[Vocab] 安全

44
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:11,644
[Host] It means safety, or safe. The opposite is danger. It works as a noun and as a describing word — a safe place, or simply safety.

45
00:05:12,244 --> 00:05:15,244
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

46
00:05:15,843 --> 00:05:18,603
[News] 今日のニュースです。

47
00:05:19,303 --> 00:05:25,855
[News] 16日の夜、関東地方で大きな地震がありました。

48
00:05:26,555 --> 00:05:34,908
[News] 午後7時46分ごろ、茨城県の南部を震源とする地震が起きました。

49
00:05:35,608 --> 00:05:42,903
[News] 群馬県と埼玉県では、最大で震度5弱を観測しました。

50
00:05:43,603 --> 00:05:49,172
[News] 強い揺れで、棚から物が落ちた家もありました。

51
00:05:49,872 --> 00:05:56,208
[News] 地震の大きさを表すマグニチュードは、5.5でした。

52
00:05:56,908 --> 00:06:01,755
[News] この地震による津波の心配はありません。

53
00:06:02,456 --> 00:06:09,824
[News] 今のところ、大きなけがや、建物の被害は報告されていません。

54
00:06:10,524 --> 00:06:19,355
[News] 気象庁は、これから1週間ほど、強い地震に注意するように呼びかけています。

55
00:06:20,055 --> 00:06:26,512
[News] 揺れの強かった地域の人は、安全に気をつけてください。

56
00:06:27,211 --> 00:06:29,947
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

57
00:06:30,548 --> 00:06:36,163
[Slow] 地震があったのは、何日の夜でしたか。

58
00:06:36,963 --> 00:06:41,019
[Host] On the evening of which day was the earthquake? The sixteenth.

59
00:06:41,620 --> 00:06:50,500
[Slow] 群馬県と埼玉県では、最大でどのくらいの震度を観測しましたか。

60
00:06:51,300 --> 00:06:57,516
[Host] What was the maximum seismic intensity measured in Gunma and Saitama? Level five-weak.

61
00:06:58,115 --> 00:07:04,139
[Slow] この地震で、津波の心配はありましたか。

62
00:07:04,939 --> 00:07:09,692
[Host] Was there any danger of a tsunami from this quake? No, there was none.

63
00:07:10,291 --> 00:07:22,675
[Host] That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

64
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:25,531
[News] また明日。
